// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded arc tangent of F64
//
// atan(x) = j pi/256 + atan(h) with h = (x - tan(j pi/256)) / (1 + x tan(j pi/256)),
// j picked from a crude quadratic in the bits of x, and a short odd polynomial
// in h; above 0x1.2ded8e34a9035p+7, atan(x) = sign(x) pi/2 + atan(-1/x), and
// small |x| takes an odd polynomial in x. When the fast path's error bound
// can't decide the rounding, the accurate path redoes it in double-double
// with 129 reduction points, and a table covers the inputs too close to a
// rounding boundary. Round to nearest only: +-0 stays itself, +-inf gives
// +-pi/2 rounded, NaN comes back quiet.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/atan/atan.c via RazorForge's B64Atan.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

